# ── Supabase Postgres (production database) ────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and replace the values. Never commit .env.
#
# From Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Database:
#
# 1) CONNECTION POOLING (recommended for Prisma / serverless / Render):
#    "Connection string" → "Transaction" / pooling enabled (port 6543).
#    Use the pgbouncer-style pooler URL so Prisma doesn't exhaust connections:
#      DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5"
#
# 2) If you prefer the direct connection, use the "Session" string on port 5432:
#      DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@db.<region>.supabase.co:5432/postgres"
#
# Important:
#   - The `-y`/`?pgbouncer=true` parameter is REQUIRED when using the pooler.
#   - Prisma DDL (migrate deploy) should run against the DIRECT connection
#     (port 5432), not the pooler. If you deploy migrations through Render,
#     either add a separate DIRECT_URL or run `npx prisma migrate deploy`
#     locally/pipeline against the direct URL, then keep DATABASE_URL pooled
#     for runtime.
#   - Keep the password URL-encoded if it contains special characters
#     (e.g. `#`, `@`, `%`).
#   - Supabase IP allow-list: if enabled, add Render's egress IPs (see
#     Network settings in the Render service) to the Supabase database
#     allow-list.